    "lawCode": "Amd §16, Mult Res L; amd §15, Mult Dwell L (as proposed in S.2294-A & A.2134-A)",
    "lawSection": "Multiple Residence Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8035\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the multiple residence law and the multiple dwelling\nlaw, in relation to requiring owners and agents of multiple residences\nand multiple dwellings to provide names and contact information of resi-\ndents to emergency personnel\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to the provisions of\nL.2023 c.635, to clarify provisions that allow public housing authori-\nties to update their residence list upon annual recertification of\ntenants.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation amends the underlying chapter by adding clarifying\nlanguage that public housing authorities may update their residence list\nupon annual recertification of tenants.\n\n \nEXISTING LAW:\n\nNone.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 635 of the Laws of 2023. S.2294-A and\nA.2134-A both passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in May 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the same date and in the same manner as a\nchapter of the laws of 2023 multiple residence law and multiple dwell-\nings law, in relation to requiring owners and agents of multiple resi-\ndences and multiple dwellings to provide names and contact information\nof residents to emergency personnel, as proposed in legislative bills\nnumbers S.2294-A and A.2134-A, takes effect.\n",
